      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Film grain honestly is really really bad when it's used at all when you have visual snow syndrome. If you ever want to know what it's like to have visual snow syndrome, it pretty much just looks like film grain, but with that effect irl, so often the post processing effect just makes symptoms worse. Ambient occlusion also is actually broken in VR and does not work very well. Some people also overuse it and it causes eye strain. I extremely agree with chromatic aberration being highest priority though because it just makes things really blurry and strains my eyes.\n\nWe really REALLY need post processing options.\n\nAlso quick edit: some people use camera blurring/lense focus stuff in their post processing or effects and it actually just looks really bad in vr.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
