  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a VR world explorer, I want to adjust and save post-processing settings for each world so that I can explore worlds and hang out with friends comfortably, without eye strain.\n\nWhen I visit a world for the first time, I want to see it exactly as the world author intended, with all post-processing effects displayed at the author's chosen intensity. At my discretion, I want to be able to dial back or disable the effects listed below, and I want my settings to be remembered for the next time I visit that world.\n\n# Bloom\n\n- **Status:** Available as a global slider, but lacking per-world control.\n\n- **Motivation:** Tasteful use of bloom can look good, but it's too intense in some worlds. Sometimes I turn off bloom in one world and then forget to turn it on again later. As a result, I miss out on tasteful uses of bloom in other worlds until I remember to reactivate it.\n\n# Chromatic Aberration\n\n- **Status:** Unavailable (highest priority).\n\n- **Motivation:** Causes uncomfortable pincushion distortion in VR.\n\n# Vignette\n\n- **Status:** Unavailable.\n\n- **Motivation:** Causes uncomfortable stereoscopic brightness differences in VR.\n\n# Ambient Occlusion\n\n- **Status:** Unavailable.\n\n- **Motivation:** Sometimes causes the eyes of anime avatars to look creepy.\n\n# Grain\n\n- **Status:** Unavailable (low priority).\n\n- **Motivation:** In rare cases, world authors overuse it.",
